    "title": "Global Daily Satellite-Derived Lake Surface Water Quality Dataset (2002-2022)",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20347115",
    "publication_date": "2026-05-22",
    "description": "<p>This repository hosts a standardized, accessible dataset of concurrent daily water quality statistics for 5,551 lakes worldwide from 2002 to 2022. Derived from the European Space Agency's Lakes Climate Change Initiative (ESA Lakes_cci) v2.1 and intersected with HydroLAKES v1.0 polygon boundaries, the dataset provides lake-wide statistics (minimum, maximum, mean, standard deviation, valid pixel count, spatial coverage ratio) for three water quality parameters: chlorophyll-a (Chl-a, mg m⁻&sup3;), lake surface water temperature (LSWT, &deg;C), and turbidity (NTU). Records are temporally harmonized to retain only days on which all three parameters are simultaneously valid. A multi-tiered QA/QC flagging scheme is included to identify spatial inhomogeneities and temporal anomalies.</p>\n<p><strong>Repository contents:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>hylak_id_description.csv</code> &mdash; 47-column summary metadata file (central coordinates, country, K&ouml;ppen-Geiger climate zone, valid observation counts, and long-term monthly/year-round means) for all 5,551 lakes.<br><br><br></li>\n<li><code>hylak_id.zip</code> &mdash; 5,551 individual CSV files (one per lake, named <code>{hylak_id}.csv</code>), each containing the 22-column daily time series with QA/QC flags.<br><br><br></li>\n<li><code>code.zip</code> &mdash; Python (v3.10) scripts used for data extraction, spatial masking, zonal statistics, harmonization, and QA/QC flagging.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Full methodology, variable definitions, and validation are described in the companion paper (DOI to be added after publication).</p>",
